WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.340
I am so happy that we are still here

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.560
with the incredible John Cena.

3
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.560
(audience cheering)

4
00:00:11.189 --> 00:00:14.522
Thank you so much for being who you are.

5
00:00:16.193 --> 00:00:19.760
Ah, man, I just wish everybody would be.

6
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.840
It's tough. It's tough.

7
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.740
Well, any advice,

8
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.573
as a parting word

9
00:00:26.573 --> 00:00:29.600
for people to have the bravery

10
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.840
to be themselves?

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.970
'Cause we all have to find it even sometimes every day.

12
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:34.803
Yeah.

13
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:36.963
Everybody,

14
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.040
especially nowadays in the realm of social sharing

15
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:44.873
and motivation.

16
00:00:44.873 --> 00:00:48.380
Everybody's pretty quick to like share quotes

17
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.623
and things.

18
00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.400
I specifically use Twitter as a forum,

19
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.563
almost like a journal of philosophy for me.

20
00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.680
But there's a reason I publish those quotes

21
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.730
instead of keeping them to myself.

22
00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.640
And that's to hold myself accountable

23
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.435
because I want to be the person I tell people that I am.

24
00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:10.268
Mm.

25
00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:12.000
So when I put something out to the universe

26
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.800
that instigates a conversation about philosophy

27
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.960
or tackles an uncomfortable subject,

28
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.173
it makes me accountable.

29
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.540
When I tell you, "I love my wife",

30
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.800
it makes me accountable.

31
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.670
She knows, I love her.

32
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.180
She doesn't need me to tell you,

33
00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.610
but it makes me accountable.

34
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.410
And I think that's important

35
00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.750
for me as a system of checks and balances

36
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.650
for the rest of the world to keep me in line.

37
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:41.650
And I just think nowadays we have the freedom of speech,

38
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.730
but we don't have any accountability

39
00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.230
a lot of times for that.

40
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:49.700
So people can tell people

41
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.290
they're a certain way and don't necessarily

42
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.860
have to walk that talk.

43
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.540
And that's hard business

44
00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.970
because you have to choose values.

45
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.110
You have to choose beliefs.

46
00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.680
You have to define purpose.

47
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.420
And you have to be honest with yourself

48
00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.840
on who you are and all of that stuff

49
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.590
is hard work.

50
00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.520
And I guess my advice is it's not easy

51
00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:14.690
'cause we all want people to see us

52
00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:17.290
as perfect folks.

53
00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.500
Just remember that everybody's flawed.

54
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.880
We all make mistakes

55
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.040
But it's hard.

56
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:25.873
It's hard work,

57
00:02:27.097 --> 00:02:28.887
but damn it's worth it.

58
00:02:28.887 --> 00:02:32.054
(audience applauding)

59
00:02:33.463 --> 00:02:36.463
(audience cheering)

60
00:02:38.356 --> 00:02:40.920
I think the world of you.

61
00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.540
Please give my absolute love to your wife.

62
00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.373
Will do.

63
00:02:44.373 --> 00:02:46.410
I don't even know how to add this,

64
00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.270
other than to say thank you.

65
00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.140
Because these are the kind of conversations

66
00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.700
that I could only hope to have on a show like this.

67
00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.600
And it takes you to have them.

68
00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.770
So, John Cena,

69
00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:02.350
his show Peacemaker is now streaming

70
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.210
only on HBOMax.

71
00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.403
It's incredible.

72
00:03:07.415 --> 00:03:09.998
(upbeat music)

